  "hints": [
    "Build a combination one candidate at a time and track how much of the target is still missing. Stop a branch when it reaches exactly 0 (record it) or goes below 0.",
    "To avoid listing [2, 3] and [3, 2] separately, only allow candidates from index start onwards. Because a candidate can be reused, recurse with start = i, not i + 1.",
    "Sort the candidates first. Then as soon as candidates[i] is bigger than what's left, every later candidate is too: break out of the loop instead of recursing."
